WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.694
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:09.964 --> 00:14.036
As expected, Baek Hee makes better mung bean pancakes than you do.

3
00:14.036 --> 00:17.546
Delicious. Let's eat together, dear.

4
00:17.546 --> 00:22.174
Family is about clashing with each other, blending together, and becoming one,

5
00:22.174 --> 00:26.438
as you told me thirty years ago.

6
00:26.438 --> 00:28.485
Even after my husband passed away,

7
00:28.485 --> 00:31.874
I always thought this was where I belonged.

8
00:31.874 --> 00:35.075
I thought I'd do my part as a daughter-in-law,

9
00:36.274 --> 00:39.288
because this was the family I chose.

10
00:41.382 --> 00:43.834
Of course, I know.

11
00:45.550 --> 00:48.882
But, Mother, and Father.

12
00:48.882 --> 00:52.302
Now, I'd like to step back as a daughter-in-law

13
00:52.302 --> 00:56.026
and step forward as a mother.

14
00:56.026 --> 00:57.458
What do you mean?

15
00:57.458 --> 01:00.378
Yeon Su and Dokgo Dal.

16
01:00.378 --> 01:02.895
I'm going to give them my blessing.

17
01:05.950 --> 01:07.366
- Baek Hee! - Yeon Su

18
01:07.366 --> 01:10.502
would never make a reckless decision.

19
01:11.462 --> 01:14.906
So I'm going to trust her.

20
01:16.230 --> 01:18.218
Because she's my daughter.

21
01:35.494 --> 01:36.738
Who is it?

22
01:36.738 --> 01:40.858
Oh, Sera, it's Yeon Su's mom.

23
01:40.858 --> 01:43.434
Oh, ma'am! What brings you here at this hour?

24
01:43.434 --> 01:46.013
Sorry to come by at this hour.

25
01:46.013 --> 01:48.150
Yeon Su hasn't been answering my calls.

26
01:48.150 --> 01:50.942
Your fridge must be empty with Yeon Su staying here, right?

27
01:50.942 --> 01:52.918
Here, I brought you some side dishes.

28
01:52.918 --> 01:55.478
- Oh... - Thanks for looking after her.

29
01:55.478 --> 01:57.202
I appreciate it.

30
01:57.202 --> 01:59.217
Looking after her?

31
02:00.162 --> 02:03.370
Oh, yes! Thank you, I'll enjoy it.

32
02:03.370 --> 02:07.266
We were already out of food, so she went out to get some chicken...

33
02:07.266 --> 02:09.306
I'll try to call her...

34
02:09.306 --> 02:10.442
Call...

35
02:10.442 --> 02:13.038
Is Yeon Su not here?

36
02:13.038 --> 02:14.733
Well...

37
02:18.702 --> 02:20.681
Sera?

38
02:21.562 --> 02:24.576
Why would she come here?

39
02:28.630 --> 02:31.750
Sera, what brings you here?

40
02:36.186 --> 02:39.049
M-Mom!

41
03:17.166 --> 03:19.302
Mom,

42
03:19.302 --> 03:21.542
I'll explain everything.

43
03:27.862 --> 03:29.630
Mom!

44
03:30.234 --> 03:32.046
Mom!

45
03:32.046 --> 03:34.966
You defied your elders and left home, and this is what you do?

46
03:34.966 --> 03:38.870
Living together? Is this why you left?

47
03:38.870 --> 03:42.126
It's not like that. I'm just staying here temporarily.

48
03:42.126 --> 03:44.781
Is this how you deal with your feelings?

49
03:45.810 --> 03:49.578
Gong Yeon Su, I'm so disappointed in you.

50
03:51.830 --> 03:55.375
Let me take you home.

51
04:00.702 --> 04:02.457
Get in.

52
04:03.826 --> 04:05.719
I said get in!

53
04:20.082 --> 04:22.360
I'm not going, Mom.

54
04:24.162 --> 04:28.870
I'll stay here until I find a place.

55
04:28.870 --> 04:31.620
Then take care on your way home.

56
04:33.426 --> 04:36.574
Sera, please take care of my mom.

57
05:27.378 --> 05:28.730
What are you doing?

58
05:29.421 --> 05:30.493
You're up?

59
05:30.493 --> 05:33.306
Let's have breakfast. Soy sauce and egg over rice.

60
05:34.422 --> 05:37.610
Oh, did you say you don't eat breakfast?

61
05:37.610 --> 05:39.963
Then just have a little taste.

62
05:51.230 --> 05:53.410
Are you okay?

63
05:53.410 --> 05:54.526
What do you mean?

64
05:54.526 --> 05:57.330
You looked like you didn't sleep a wink last night.

65
05:59.530 --> 06:02.690
I'm going to start looking for a place today.

66
06:02.690 --> 06:04.518
I hope I can find somewhere decent.

67
06:04.518 --> 06:07.474
Have you really made up your mind?

68
06:07.474 --> 06:09.298
Yes.

69
06:10.098 --> 06:13.014
Why? Do I seem unprepared?

70
06:13.014 --> 06:14.106
That's not what I meant.

71
06:14.106 --> 06:19.450
It's something I have to face sooner or later.

72
06:19.450 --> 06:22.842
I'm stepping outside the safety of the life I've always known.

73
06:22.842 --> 06:27.385
Of course, I'm bound to get a few scrapes.

74
06:31.102 --> 06:33.762
[Final Episode]

75
06:38.726 --> 06:40.218
That ungrateful punk.

76
06:40.218 --> 06:41.998
When an elder gives an inch,

77
06:41.998 --> 06:45.062
she should just say, "Thank you," and accept it.

78
06:45.062 --> 06:47.934
This is why they say raising daughters is pointless.

79
06:47.934 --> 06:50.878
Ugh, why are my ears burning?

80
06:50.878 --> 06:53.810
Baek Hee, you talk some sense into her.

81
06:53.810 --> 06:57.981
You know, she can date someone without moving out.

82
07:00.218 --> 07:01.514
Nam Su, you too!

83
07:01.514 --> 07:04.362
I'll arrange a match as soon as your exam is over. Just so you know.

84
07:04.362 --> 07:06.586
Oh, you mean Professor Eom's second daughter?

85
07:06.586 --> 07:08.114
- Is she an elementary school teacher? - Yes.

86
07:08.114 --> 07:11.438
Come on, why is everyone in such a hurry?

87
07:11.438 --> 07:14.278
Can't we see how things go before rushing into...

88
07:14.278 --> 07:16.166
- What things? - Doesn't Professor Eom's daughter

89
07:16.166 --> 07:17.650
get a say in what she wants too?

90
07:17.650 --> 07:18.672
Quiet!

91
07:18.672 --> 07:21.746
A handsome face and a grade-seven civil service job? He's a top-tier catch!

92
07:21.746 --> 07:24.158
- Exactly. - Well...

93
07:24.158 --> 07:25.638
Grandpa.

94
07:25.638 --> 07:27.412
What?

95
07:28.494 --> 07:33.243
I'd like to put off my exam for just one year.

96
07:35.686 --> 07:37.546
- What? - Nam Su!

97
07:37.546 --> 07:39.614
Why are you doing this too?

98
07:39.614 --> 07:43.706
They say when your heart is unsettled, you lose your way.

99
07:43.706 --> 07:47.226
I just want one year to get my feelings in order.

100
07:47.226 --> 07:50.469
Don't you care about your mother, who's been supporting you through this exam?

101
07:50.469 --> 07:51.998
An unsettled heart?

102
07:51.998 --> 07:54.781
Isn't it your head that's all messed up?

103
07:57.934 --> 08:00.002
Nam Su.

104
08:00.002 --> 08:02.439
If you don't pass this exam,

105
08:03.670 --> 08:05.290
you're out too.

106
08:05.290 --> 08:07.250
Oh, here you go again.

107
08:07.250 --> 08:09.718
I don't need anyone who goes against me!

108
08:09.718 --> 08:13.091
If you want to do things your own way, then get out! All of you!

109
08:14.270 --> 08:15.972
Really?

110
08:17.394 --> 08:21.610
Then does that mean I can move out too?

111
08:21.610 --> 08:23.542
Move out?

112
08:24.578 --> 08:28.310
Are you all staging some kind of independence movement or what?

113
08:28.310 --> 08:29.422
Baek Hee!

114
08:29.422 --> 08:31.302
- Oh, yes. - Clear the table!

115
08:32.269 --> 08:33.906
No way...

116
08:33.906 --> 08:37.154
It's been a while. I think I'll paint some orchids.

117
08:38.733 --> 08:40.702
G-Grandpa!

118
08:55.790 --> 08:59.654
Grandpa... when are you going to paint them?

119
09:07.926 --> 09:09.981
The ink's too diluted.

120
09:19.830 --> 09:21.290
Godal.

121
09:21.290 --> 09:25.480
Aren't you practically a traitor to that family by now?

122
09:26.102 --> 09:27.254
What did Ms. Yeon Su say?

123
09:27.254 --> 09:29.710
I think she's made up her mind.

124
09:29.710 --> 09:31.526
She's moving out.

125
09:33.069 --> 09:38.106
- You really are a traitor. - I don't care if I'm a traitor or a thief.

126
09:38.106 --> 09:42.038
I'm just worried she might end up...

127
09:42.038 --> 09:44.516
estranged from her family because of me.

128
09:45.570 --> 09:47.794
Why would that be your fault?

129
09:49.258 --> 09:51.310
Fine, say they do grow apart.

130
09:51.310 --> 09:53.198
But that's Ms. Yeon Su's choice.

131
09:53.198 --> 09:56.258
You have nothing to feel guilty about. You're both adults.

132
09:56.258 --> 10:02.350
Love makes you do things you'd never normally do. It makes you impulsive.

133
10:02.998 --> 10:05.562
Good grief. Both you and Ms. Yeon Su.

134
10:05.562 --> 10:06.818
- Me? - Yeah.

135
10:06.818 --> 10:09.842
- You're doing the same thing right now. - I am?

136
10:09.842 --> 10:11.489
You can't stand having people around for more than a day.

137
10:11.489 --> 10:13.362
You even kicked me out.

138
10:13.362 --> 10:17.046
But how many days have you been living with her now? Doesn't she bother you?

139
10:17.046 --> 10:19.114
You're not annoyed?

140
10:19.114 --> 10:21.798
Seriously? That's hurtful.

141
10:21.798 --> 10:24.222
Tell me. Is it me or Ms. Yeon Su?

142
10:24.222 --> 10:25.610
- Well... - Hey, stop! Stop!

143
10:25.610 --> 10:27.290
Don't say it. I don't wanna hear it.

144
10:28.762 --> 10:31.670
No, come on. Tell me.

145
10:31.670 --> 10:33.381
I'm confident.

146
10:34.086 --> 10:36.710
- Really? - You just answered with your eyebrows.

147
10:36.710 --> 10:39.086
Let's go.

148
10:39.086 --> 10:41.778
- Where are you going? - To get something to eat.

149
10:41.778 --> 10:45.394
- I'm not eating! - Why aren't you eating? Don't like it?

150
10:45.394 --> 10:47.674
Want something else?

151
10:47.674 --> 10:51.290
It's fine. I'm really okay, Sera.

152
10:51.290 --> 10:53.758
I'm just worried you're feeling bad.

153
10:53.758 --> 10:57.702
Do you know how hard I prayed that door wouldn't open that day?

154
10:57.702 --> 11:02.285
But how did you even know where he lived?

155
11:02.285 --> 11:06.214
You two had no connection outside of work, right?

156
11:06.214 --> 11:08.066
Oh, that's...

157
11:08.066 --> 11:11.854
There's actually one connection you don't know about.

158
11:11.854 --> 11:14.150
A connection I don't know about?

159
11:18.013 --> 11:20.738
Oh, I wasn't trying to hide it from you.

160
11:20.738 --> 11:26.029
You know I reveal their existence, but never their identities, right?

161
11:26.925 --> 11:29.410
You left me all alone in Busan,

162
11:29.410 --> 11:32.829
but you were with Min Hyeong all along?

163
11:32.829 --> 11:36.682
You weren't exactly alone either!

164
11:36.682 --> 11:40.438
So, is it over between you two now?

165
11:40.438 --> 11:43.062
Well, he did graduate, but...

166
11:43.062 --> 11:44.198
But?

167
11:44.198 --> 11:46.466
Sera, now that I've graduated,

168
11:46.466 --> 11:48.634
how about we get to know each other as equals?

169
11:48.634 --> 11:50.334
What is there to know?

170
11:50.334 --> 11:52.810
You know how dangerous a younger guy can be

171
11:53.662 --> 11:56.450
when he falls in love late, right?

172
11:56.450 --> 12:00.534
You know, right? I don't do relationships.

173
12:00.534 --> 12:03.346
You know me. I only do casual flings too.

174
12:03.346 --> 12:06.674
A more long-term fling, maybe?

175
12:06.674 --> 12:11.322
True! You don't have to label a relationship as dating.

176
12:11.322 --> 12:14.333
Gong Yeon Su... What are you?

177
12:14.333 --> 12:15.470
- What? - "In that case,

178
12:15.470 --> 12:17.518
you might as well just date, Sera."

179
12:17.518 --> 12:19.612
Why aren't you saying that?

180
12:20.266 --> 12:22.654
Well, I guess you two will figure it out yourselves.

181
12:22.654 --> 12:24.674
There's no one right way to have a relationship.

182
12:24.674 --> 12:27.620
Sera, try this. It's good.

183
12:32.694 --> 12:35.962
Where on earth are you? Si Eun...

184
12:42.862 --> 12:45.455
[Sun Hee's]

185
12:55.918 --> 12:57.038
Oh, it's hot!

186
12:57.038 --> 13:00.002
Are you okay? You're not hurt?

187
13:00.830 --> 13:04.507
Si Eun, move back a little. I'll grill it.

188
13:08.862 --> 13:10.706
That looks good.

189
13:15.170 --> 13:18.826
Try it. It should be really juicy.

190
13:19.565 --> 13:22.298
- Good, right? - It's so good! Seriously delicious!

191
13:22.298 --> 13:23.902
Try this one later too.

192
13:28.877 --> 13:32.398
- Is it good? - Have some too. Don't give it all to me.

193
13:32.398 --> 13:35.455
I don't know why I love feeding you so much.

194
13:36.886 --> 13:39.000
- It's good! - Right?

195
13:53.510 --> 13:55.778
Why is everything so good?

196
14:15.238 --> 14:18.031
[1:1 Consultation, Will this really help our sex life?]

197
14:20.714 --> 14:24.358
Have you given it to your wife yet?

198
14:24.358 --> 14:28.126
I'm sorry, but it's unused. Can I get a refund?

199
14:28.126 --> 14:29.650
A refund?

200
14:29.650 --> 14:31.946
I finally worked up the nerve to buy it,

201
14:31.946 --> 14:34.706
but I can't bring myself to use it.

202
14:35.586 --> 14:41.729
Do you have the courage to have an honest talk with your wife?

203
14:45.454 --> 14:47.330
I'm not sure.

204
14:47.330 --> 14:49.737
Maybe someday, if the chance comes...

205
14:58.210 --> 14:59.290
Hello?

206
14:59.290 --> 15:01.206
Let's do it now.

207
15:01.206 --> 15:02.365
What are you talking about?

208
15:02.365 --> 15:06.622
What do you mean, "someday"? When is that?

209
15:06.622 --> 15:09.854
I'm saying let's do it now.

210
15:09.854 --> 15:11.998
Let's be brave.

211
15:11.998 --> 15:13.902
Well...

212
15:13.902 --> 15:17.498
The place we always went. I'll wait for you there.

213
15:24.846 --> 15:26.262
Since when?

214
15:26.262 --> 15:28.568
Oh, when was it?

215
15:30.050 --> 15:35.141
Around the time you left your job?

216
16:02.278 --> 16:04.613
[Indulge in whole-body orgasms]

217
16:06.926 --> 16:09.191
You're not going to return it, are you?

218
16:16.902 --> 16:18.609
That's not fair.

219
16:54.386 --> 16:56.264
Why isn't she coming?

220
16:57.458 --> 17:00.785
If I'd known, I would've gone to pick her up.

221
17:01.982 --> 17:03.738
She's here!

222
17:07.130 --> 17:09.478
- You're here? - You scared me!

223
17:09.478 --> 17:11.362
- Are you going somewhere? - No.

224
17:11.362 --> 17:13.866
Why are you standing there?

225
17:13.866 --> 17:14.930
I was getting some water.

226
17:15.965 --> 17:18.035
Getting water by the front door?

227
17:21.058 --> 17:23.541
And where's your other shoe?

228
17:36.861 --> 17:38.102
Did you check out some places?

229
17:38.102 --> 17:41.338
I saw a few, but I need to look at more.

230
17:41.338 --> 17:43.778
Did you look around here, by any chance?

231
17:43.778 --> 17:45.498
Near your place?

232
17:45.498 --> 17:49.242
Yeah, this area's great. It's got good amenities too.

233
17:53.830 --> 17:56.424
But the prices aren't great.

234
18:01.058 --> 18:03.590
- Where are you going? - To get some water.

235
18:03.590 --> 18:05.874
I'll get it for you.

236
18:05.874 --> 18:07.942
Lukewarm water, please.

237
18:07.942 --> 18:09.929
Sure, got it!

238
18:18.365 --> 18:19.853
Where are you going?

239
18:19.853 --> 18:21.434
Tissues...

240
18:30.682 --> 18:32.451
Why?

241
18:33.234 --> 18:36.877
Now that I look at you, you're secretly clingy, huh?

242
18:36.877 --> 18:38.386
I'm not.

243
18:39.314 --> 18:41.181
You are!

244
18:45.690 --> 18:47.298
It's not so bad.

245
18:47.298 --> 18:50.141
When I've heard "Where are you" and "Where are you going" all my life,

246
18:50.141 --> 18:52.505
it felt like nagging.

247
18:54.813 --> 18:57.693
Guess I won't hear that anymore.

248
19:00.474 --> 19:02.358
But I...

249
19:02.358 --> 19:07.810
I don't want you to give up anything precious because of me, Yeon Su.

250
19:07.810 --> 19:08.910
Anything precious?

251
19:08.910 --> 19:12.900
Like turning your back on your family?

252
19:13.706 --> 19:17.122
Have I turned my back on my family?

253
19:17.122 --> 19:20.818
I may have taken a step back, but I haven't turned my back on them.

254
19:20.818 --> 19:25.598
You haven't? You fought with them, left home, and now you're here with me.

255
19:33.026 --> 19:36.734
I like you, Dokgo Dal.

256
19:36.734 --> 19:40.490
But the reason I'm moving out is

257
19:40.490 --> 19:45.190
that I've finally found the strength to stand by my choices.

258
19:45.190 --> 19:49.422
I want to live by my own standards, not someone else's.

259
19:49.422 --> 19:52.982
I want to take responsibility for my own life.

260
19:58.934 --> 20:01.678
So don't carry unnecessary guilt.

261
20:01.678 --> 20:05.911
Just tell me, "You'll do great."

262
20:11.754 --> 20:14.103
What is it now?

263
20:16.474 --> 20:18.498
Just...

264
20:18.498 --> 20:20.346
You're pretty.

265
20:26.462 --> 20:28.430
What are you saying?

266
20:43.810 --> 20:45.634
Oh, come on.

267
20:46.806 --> 20:49.770
I'll give you one more chance, one more.

268
20:49.770 --> 20:51.149
Here.

269
20:59.792 --> 21:02.176
[My Sini]

270
21:04.282 --> 21:06.162
Where are you?

271
21:20.002 --> 21:21.962
Kang Si Eun!

272
21:27.352 --> 21:29.319
Nam Su!

273
21:31.270 --> 21:33.349
You really...

274
21:35.026 --> 21:36.802
I'm sorry...

275
21:37.462 --> 21:39.229
I'm sorry.

276
21:40.950 --> 21:43.300
I can't give up dancing.

277
21:44.634 --> 21:47.010
But I don't want to give up our baby either.

278
21:47.010 --> 21:50.166
- Si Eun! - Why do I have to choose between the two?

279
21:50.166 --> 21:53.078
Giving up my dream to have a baby, or giving up the baby to chase my dream,

280
21:53.078 --> 21:54.909
I can't do that.

281
21:54.909 --> 21:58.494
I could do both well, right?

282
21:58.494 --> 22:00.401
I've made up my mind.

283
22:01.546 --> 22:02.594
This is my answer.

284
22:02.594 --> 22:04.670
Can I say it now?

285
22:06.370 --> 22:11.078
Si Eun, there's an old saying, "When hearts join, words become the way."

286
22:11.078 --> 22:14.081
When two hearts are one, they find a way.

287
22:14.081 --> 22:15.128
And with determination, in the end...

288
22:15.128 --> 22:16.656
Nam Su.

289
22:16.656 --> 22:18.552
Put it simply.

290
22:19.162 --> 22:21.055
I love you.

291
22:25.758 --> 22:27.954
Nam Su, I burned myself here.

292
22:27.954 --> 22:29.510
Where? How did that happen?

293
22:29.510 --> 22:30.826
A shell popped and splashed me.

294
22:30.826 --> 22:33.154
Oh, no! Does it hurt?

295
22:33.154 --> 22:35.550
- It hurts. - It does?

296
22:39.174 --> 22:43.542
Why'd you pack so much? It's heavy.

297
22:43.542 --> 22:46.322
Your brother used to like rice cakes, you know.

298
22:47.053 --> 22:49.357
You're probably the only one who still celebrates his anniversary

299
22:49.357 --> 22:52.062
after being widowed.

300
22:52.062 --> 22:55.270
Every year, without fail, with the kids.

301
22:55.270 --> 22:57.254
Where are the kids?

302
22:58.306 --> 23:01.470
I wonder what things would've been like if he were still here.

303
23:01.470 --> 23:05.634
Those kids would've gotten a proper talking-to!

304
23:05.634 --> 23:06.696
Well, who knows?

305
23:06.696 --> 23:10.270
Maybe he'd surprisingly let Yeon Su go, pretending not to know.

306
23:10.270 --> 23:13.822
Well, he always had a soft spot for Yeon Su.

307
23:13.822 --> 23:15.790
Maybe.

308
23:15.790 --> 23:19.774
If he were still around, things might never have come to this.

309
23:19.774 --> 23:23.662
You never know. I have a dad, and look how I turned out.

310
23:24.874 --> 23:27.442
Please make sure the two of them eat later.

311
23:27.442 --> 23:30.632
Oh, don't worry about that.

312
23:31.866 --> 23:35.546
Mother, Father, I'll be back.

313
23:35.546 --> 23:37.254
We'll have to order pizza for lunch.

314
23:37.254 --> 23:39.074
Go ahead.

315
24:05.202 --> 24:09.488
I've got something important to do, so I'm heading out. Make sure you eat.

316
24:14.462 --> 24:15.970
- Yeah. - Where are you?

317
24:15.970 --> 24:17.486
At home.

318
24:17.486 --> 24:19.462
- Are you alone? - Why do you ask?

319
24:19.462 --> 24:22.166
Yeon Su's grandfather called me.

320
24:22.166 --> 24:24.390
He said the house feels empty and lonely.

321
24:24.390 --> 24:26.688
He asked if we could play a round of Go.

322
24:27.310 --> 24:29.230
- So? - I said alright.

323
24:29.230 --> 24:31.998
- Yoon Jio! - I didn't say who was coming, though.

324
24:31.998 --> 24:34.364
- What? - Just thought you should know.

325
24:34.364 --> 24:36.348
I'm hanging up.

326
24:48.270 --> 24:50.487
It's been a while, Dad.

327
24:56.082 --> 24:58.537
Looks like I'm the first one here.

328
24:59.594 --> 25:03.814
This year, we're all coming at different times.

329
25:03.814 --> 25:06.128
Hope you understand, Dad.

330
25:24.046 --> 25:28.542
Father, Yeon Su and Nam Su have no shortage of marriage prospects.

331
25:28.542 --> 25:31.670
So why can't I find someone to remarry?

332
25:33.494 --> 25:36.990
Are you actually serious about this?

333
25:36.990 --> 25:38.318
If you are, I'll look into it.

334
25:38.318 --> 25:41.418
It's not just that I mean it. I think about it all day long.

335
25:41.418 --> 25:44.566
Well, I'm still young, so I should find a partner.

336
25:44.566 --> 25:46.254
You're almost 50. How is that young?

337
25:46.254 --> 25:47.958
What do you mean, almost 50?

338
25:47.958 --> 25:51.798
I'm still young enough to get pregnant if I push it!

339
25:51.798 --> 25:54.786
Oh, whatever. Both grandkids are going to leave anyway.

340
25:54.786 --> 25:57.138
Father, want me to give you a new grandchild?

341
25:57.138 --> 25:58.445
- Enough! - Jeez!

342
26:03.246 --> 26:05.154
Why do you keep showing up?

343
26:05.154 --> 26:06.506
I'm here to learn Go.

344
26:06.506 --> 26:08.774
You came at a good time.

345
26:08.774 --> 26:12.438
We're having a meal. Join us.

346
26:12.438 --> 26:15.154
- Mi Young! - Yes.

347
26:15.154 --> 26:17.024
Clear the table!

348
26:29.018 --> 26:32.314
You seem to have plenty of free time, huh?

349
26:32.314 --> 26:34.814
What, is your adult toy business slow?

350
26:34.814 --> 26:37.538
Business is great. My capable staff keep things running

351
26:37.538 --> 26:39.246
just fine without me.

352
26:39.246 --> 26:41.458
You never lose a word, do you? Not one word.

353
26:41.458 --> 26:45.294
So, have you been in touch with Yeon Su lately?

354
26:45.294 --> 26:50.274
That girl has never caused me this much worry before.

355
26:50.274 --> 26:52.765
Our sixth-generation grandmother

356
26:52.765 --> 26:55.694
even received a commendation gate for her chastity.

357
26:55.694 --> 26:58.173
And that's not all. Our fourth-generation grandmother

358
26:58.173 --> 27:01.430
even had a virtue monument built next to Seocheon Village!

359
27:01.430 --> 27:05.597
And now some guy has come and ruined it all!

360
27:07.414 --> 27:09.226
Yeon Su is simply

361
27:09.226 --> 27:13.090
taking a step forward in her own life.

362
27:13.090 --> 27:14.913
- What? - To be honest, I'm a little disappointed

363
27:14.913 --> 27:17.926
to come second in her priorities.

364
27:17.926 --> 27:22.055
But that's also one of the reasons I love her.

365
27:25.926 --> 27:30.562
I admire Yeon Su's strength and integrity.

366
27:30.562 --> 27:36.150
Her self-confidence, strong values, and good manners.

367
27:36.150 --> 27:40.610
She has a rare sense of decency that sets her apart.

368
27:40.610 --> 27:45.220
She probably learned it from her grandfather and grandmother.

369
27:48.706 --> 27:53.362
I have never once taken Yeon Su lightly.

370
27:53.362 --> 27:55.305
Oh, my.

371
28:02.234 --> 28:04.266
What are you waiting for? Make your move.

372
28:04.266 --> 28:06.325
Oh, yes.

373
28:24.138 --> 28:27.804
You're not bad at this.

374
28:32.090 --> 28:34.169
I'd better get going.

375
28:37.830 --> 28:40.146
Come visit again next time.

376
28:40.146 --> 28:43.510
Oh, and... there's something I'd like to tell you.

377
28:43.510 --> 28:45.514
Could I have a word?

378
28:48.718 --> 28:50.654
Actually...

379
28:55.270 --> 28:57.450
Then I'll really be going now.

380
28:57.450 --> 29:00.602
Yeah, get home safely.

381
29:10.254 --> 29:12.386
- You're pretty good. - Pardon?

382
29:12.386 --> 29:14.829
You got my father to paint orchids.

383
29:15.437 --> 29:16.758
It's nothing like that.

384
29:16.758 --> 29:19.162
You should learn Go in advance.

385
29:19.162 --> 29:22.898
No! Actually, don't. It's exhausting.

386
29:22.898 --> 29:26.782
By the way, I don't see Yeon Su's mother. Where did she go?

387
29:26.782 --> 29:29.046
Oh, that's...

388
29:29.046 --> 29:32.258
It's a special day today, so she went to visit my brother's grave.

389
29:32.258 --> 29:34.146
Yeon Su didn't tell you?

390
29:38.270 --> 29:41.578
I've found a few places.

391
29:41.578 --> 29:44.674
About 15 minutes from home?

392
29:44.674 --> 29:47.784
It has to be close, so we can see each other often.

393
29:50.238 --> 29:52.354
Not much will change.

394
29:52.354 --> 29:55.994
I'll still come for holidays, birthdays,

395
29:55.994 --> 29:59.149
Parents' Day, and memorial rites.

396
29:59.149 --> 30:01.089
And I'll call often too.

397
30:04.010 --> 30:05.927
Yeon Su.

398
30:09.042 --> 30:11.224
Let me ask you one thing.

399
30:13.506 --> 30:16.313
While you lived in this house,

400
30:17.442 --> 30:19.524
were you very lonely?

401
30:29.466 --> 30:33.455
It's not fair for you to ask me that, Mom.

402
30:35.118 --> 30:37.100
No one in that house

403
30:38.170 --> 30:41.338
could've been lonelier than you.

404
30:46.602 --> 30:48.637
But you know,

405
30:49.662 --> 30:53.100
it was all my choice.

406
30:57.250 --> 31:02.030
Three years was more than enough. You've done your duty, Baek Hee.

407
31:02.030 --> 31:05.974
Don't waste your youth looking after us old folks.

408
31:05.974 --> 31:09.508
Go out and live freely.

409
31:10.234 --> 31:16.762
Well, when you put it that way, I feel a little hurt.

410
31:16.762 --> 31:21.390
Father, Mother, you're the first family I've ever chosen for myself.

411
31:21.390 --> 31:26.654
Whether my husband is here or not, I'll remain this family's daughter-in-law

412
31:26.654 --> 31:29.553
and a member of the family.

413
31:30.202 --> 31:32.910
I was lonely, sure,

414
31:32.910 --> 31:35.951
but I wasn't always lonely.

415
31:36.670 --> 31:39.206
The reason I chose to stay in that house

416
31:39.206 --> 31:42.899
wasn't duty, but my heart.

417
31:45.646 --> 31:51.116
I wanted to raise you both within the safety of a family.

418
31:53.405 --> 31:57.770
But I never realized that it might end up trapping you instead.

419
31:57.770 --> 32:00.562
Mom, remember what you told me

420
32:00.562 --> 32:05.114
when you put my hairpin in my hair on my 20th birthday?

421
32:05.114 --> 32:06.578
This hairpin

422
32:06.578 --> 32:11.758
is the burden you must shoulder as a woman.

423
32:11.758 --> 32:18.318
From now on, you must stay modest and prudent in both body and mind.

424
32:18.318 --> 32:23.418
Back then, that hairpin felt so heavy.

425
32:27.058 --> 32:30.826
But looking back, I think its weight

426
32:30.826 --> 32:33.950
kept me grounded.

427
32:35.466 --> 32:39.410
So you weren't trapping us, Mom.

428
32:39.410 --> 32:41.138
You were protecting us.

429
32:41.138 --> 32:45.730
We've just grown enough that we don't need

430
32:45.730 --> 32:49.194
that fence anymore, that's all.

431
32:49.194 --> 32:54.346
Just as you followed your heart back then,

432
32:55.130 --> 32:59.492
I'll follow mine from now on too.

433
33:01.662 --> 33:04.564
I didn't realize

434
33:05.262 --> 33:08.610
how well my little girl had grown up.

435
33:10.002 --> 33:12.730
Of course!

436
33:12.730 --> 33:15.325
I'm your pride and joy.

437
33:19.242 --> 33:21.206
You heard that, honey?

438
33:28.230 --> 33:33.398
[Tomb of Haeseong, Gong Seok Jun]

439
33:34.954 --> 33:38.062
- It's raining! - What's with this sudden rain?

440
33:38.062 --> 33:42.922
Oh, dear. Your dad must be sulking because Nam Su didn't come.

441
33:42.922 --> 33:44.826
I know.

442
33:44.826 --> 33:47.254
Good grief!

443
33:48.141 --> 33:50.002
It's coming down hard. Careful, Mom!

444
33:50.002 --> 33:51.519
Oh, dear, why does it keep raining?

445
33:51.519 --> 33:52.610
Mom, let me carry that.

446
33:52.610 --> 33:56.241
- It's fine I'll carry it. It's fine! - But it's heavy!

447
33:58.318 --> 34:00.720
Dokgo Dal?

448
34:02.442 --> 34:04.618
Let's get in the car first. Let me take that.

449
34:04.618 --> 34:06.698
- Oh, no, it's fine. - No, no.

450
34:15.446 --> 34:18.349
How did you know we are here?

451
34:18.349 --> 34:20.090
Your aunt told me.

452
34:20.090 --> 34:21.690
You went to our house?

453
34:21.690 --> 34:23.382
I did.

454
34:24.077 --> 34:26.366
Are you cold? Want a blanket?

455
34:26.366 --> 34:29.350
Oh, I'm fine. I have one.

456
34:29.350 --> 34:31.478
- Oh, my. - Why?

457
34:31.478 --> 34:32.670
Don't tell me you left it behind?

458
34:32.670 --> 34:35.430
Yeah, I did. Oh, no!

459
34:35.430 --> 34:36.542
I'll go get it.

460
34:36.542 --> 34:38.314
Oh, no. I'll go.

461
34:38.314 --> 34:42.014
Oh, no! You don't know where it is. I'll be right back.

462
34:42.637 --> 34:45.393
Then let's go together.

463
34:45.393 --> 34:47.300
Okay.

464
35:25.590 --> 35:28.041
So that's why you made it rain?

465
35:29.578 --> 35:33.421
He looks just like you. Just like you when you were young.

466
35:43.474 --> 35:47.786
Oh, dear. Why is it suddenly raining again?

467
35:51.649 --> 35:53.478
Did something good happen?

468
35:53.478 --> 35:56.550
You don't need to know.

469
35:59.242 --> 36:02.550
Actually, I don't have any issue in that regard.

470
36:10.338 --> 36:13.186
I'm Lee Yu Ri from the Brand Planning Team at Hyeonseong Department Store.

471
36:13.186 --> 36:14.610
[Lee Yu Ri]

472
36:14.610 --> 36:17.132
I'm Yoon Jio, VP of Loand.

473
36:22.058 --> 36:25.182
With a test store, the initial response is crucial.

474
36:25.182 --> 36:27.834
Customer feedback goes straight into our internal evaluation.

475
36:29.005 --> 36:31.818
Then the opening week is basically our report card.

476
36:31.818 --> 36:33.794
- I'm confident. - But...

477
36:33.794 --> 36:37.650
I think "pleasure" might have trouble passing review because of its connotations.

478
36:37.650 --> 36:39.654
But could you submit it for review anyway?

479
36:39.654 --> 36:41.786
If it's rejected, we'll go with Plan B.

480
36:41.786 --> 36:44.962
Your email even had a Plan C.

481
36:44.962 --> 36:47.314
Only the promotion keywords go up to C.

482
36:47.314 --> 36:52.418
Well, the product list and interior designs go up to... F, I think?

483
36:52.418 --> 36:54.218
Are you an ENFJ by any chance?

484
36:54.218 --> 36:56.726
Yes! Are you one too?

485
36:56.726 --> 37:00.562
Yes! I'm an ENFJ too.

486
37:00.562 --> 37:02.762
Wow, what a coincidence!

487
37:02.762 --> 37:05.044
- Shall we grab lunch first? - CEO?

488
37:05.044 --> 37:09.234
- Shall we? - Could you look over this vendor's proposal?

489
37:10.911 --> 37:15.162
- Oh, honey, yeah! - Oh, my stomach suddenly...

490
37:15.162 --> 37:18.234
You're hungry? Yeah, yeah.

491
37:19.578 --> 37:20.682
What do you like?

492
37:20.682 --> 37:22.314
Anything's fine.

493
37:22.314 --> 37:25.162
Oh! Except one thing. Chicken with lacquer tree bark!

494
37:25.162 --> 37:28.202
- Huh? Wait, me too! - Really?

495
37:28.202 --> 37:30.978
I once ended up in the ER after eating it.

496
37:30.978 --> 37:34.292
Oh, wow. Me, too! I swelled up so bad.

497
37:45.378 --> 37:47.198
How's the Hyeonseong deal coming along?

498
37:47.198 --> 37:48.738
Where'd you hear about that?

499
37:48.738 --> 37:50.630
It's not like it's some big secret.

500
37:50.630 --> 37:52.602
It's still in progress.

501
37:53.622 --> 37:55.939
What about you and her? Still living together?

502
37:57.878 --> 38:00.278
Or did you break up?

503
38:00.278 --> 38:03.570
- No. - You actually brought a woman home.

504
38:03.570 --> 38:05.330
She must be something special.

505
38:05.330 --> 38:09.118
You said you didn't want to hurt someone precious to you.

506
38:10.614 --> 38:12.562
Don't make that face.

507
38:12.562 --> 38:15.708
I'm not against it. I was just curious.

508
38:20.118 --> 38:23.550
I'm going to try not to hurt her.

509
38:25.542 --> 38:27.887
I've come to want to make that effort.

510
38:32.690 --> 38:35.038
Don't worry.

511
38:35.038 --> 38:37.202
You're not like me.

512
38:37.202 --> 38:40.251
At least you won't go around setting your kid up

513
38:40.251 --> 38:44.904
with women just to find them a suitable mom.

514
38:49.006 --> 38:50.822
That child has a sadness about him.

515
38:50.822 --> 38:53.901
Why does someone so young have such sad eyes?

516
38:55.030 --> 38:57.226
[Divorce Papers] He can feed himself.

517
38:57.226 --> 38:59.434
I didn't marry to cook for him.

518
38:59.434 --> 39:01.554
See how he behaves and then decide.

519
39:01.554 --> 39:05.258
You haven't already transferred the property to him, have you?

520
39:05.998 --> 39:09.012
Call and ask him to come over for a meal.

521
39:10.030 --> 39:11.665
It's still his birthday.

522
39:11.665 --> 39:14.142
Forget it. Who needs a meal?

523
39:23.282 --> 39:24.442
Eat up.

524
39:24.442 --> 39:26.158
You're paying anyway.

525
39:26.158 --> 39:27.670
- Me? - Of course, you are.

526
39:27.670 --> 39:30.226
You're making good money these days.

527
39:30.226 --> 39:34.626
Have you tried her cooking? She's a great cook.

528
39:34.626 --> 39:39.050
Really? I'll... pay today.

529
39:39.050 --> 39:40.318
Really?

530
39:40.318 --> 39:41.414
Yes.

531
39:42.893 --> 39:44.839
Look at you, son. All grown up.

532
39:45.758 --> 39:47.967
Could you bring it over here?

533
39:49.086 --> 39:51.226
You can put it down here.

534
39:51.226 --> 39:53.598
Oh, just a little this way!

535
40:07.002 --> 40:08.046
Yeah, Sera.

536
40:08.046 --> 40:11.294
How is it? How does standing on your own feel?

537
40:11.294 --> 40:14.786
It's nice. It really is, but...

538
40:16.722 --> 40:21.438
Ugh, you have to set it down gently! It's all broken...

539
40:21.438 --> 40:23.837
I think I moved a little too close.

540
40:23.837 --> 40:26.722
What should I get you for your housewarming?

541
40:26.722 --> 40:29.186
Anything. Thanks.

542
40:29.186 --> 40:31.761
Alright, I'll talk to you again.

543
40:34.970 --> 40:36.366
On the day of the first snow,

544
40:36.366 --> 40:40.398
I finally had a space of my own for the first time.

545
40:40.398 --> 40:42.010
- Oh! It hurts. Oh, I got a cramp! - Why, what?

546
40:42.010 --> 40:44.150
What? A cramp? Where? Where? Here? Here?

547
40:44.150 --> 40:45.926
Oh... just kidding.

548
40:45.926 --> 40:50.296
Sera continued her long, undefined fling.

549
40:51.382 --> 40:53.132
[Encyclopedia of Pregnancy, Childbirth, and Childcare]

550
40:57.170 --> 40:59.972
Oh! Be careful!

551
41:05.310 --> 41:07.090
[Civil Servant ID, Gong Nam Su] Is the bed a little small?

552
41:07.090 --> 41:08.730
Too small? Should we get a bigger one?

553
41:08.730 --> 41:10.554
It might be a little low too.

554
41:10.554 --> 41:12.902
Too low? Should we get a taller one?

555
41:12.902 --> 41:14.654
Ugh, I can't say anything around you.

556
41:14.654 --> 41:16.259
Oh, my little baby!

557
41:16.259 --> 41:18.094
Let Nam Su handle all this stuff.

558
41:18.094 --> 41:22.758
Baby, you sit right here and eat this!

559
41:22.758 --> 41:24.540
Thank you.

560
41:26.586 --> 41:28.187
- Where's Grandpa? - Yes, he went to the market

561
41:28.187 --> 41:31.234
to buy shellfish for our baby.

562
41:31.234 --> 41:34.508
The day Nam Su announced he was going to be a father...

563
41:34.508 --> 41:37.358
What? A f-f-father?

564
41:42.770 --> 41:44.290
- Father! Father! - Grandpa!

565
41:44.290 --> 41:45.994
911! Call 911!

566
41:45.994 --> 41:48.558
- Grandpa collapsed from high blood pressure. - 911! Oh, no, Grandpa.

567
41:48.558 --> 41:50.630
Please wake up...

568
41:50.630 --> 41:53.118
And then, fortunately...

569
41:53.118 --> 41:55.094
It's a boy.

570
41:56.414 --> 41:59.140
A-A boy?

571
42:02.822 --> 42:04.670
Baek Hee, bring me some water.

572
42:04.670 --> 42:06.472
Yes, Father.

573
42:08.338 --> 42:11.386
Mi Young, you know Carl Sagan, right?

574
42:11.386 --> 42:13.240
- Carl Se... - Cosmos, the thick book.

575
42:13.240 --> 42:14.276
Oh, yes. Right.

576
42:14.276 --> 42:15.918
The universe is enormous, right?

577
42:15.918 --> 42:18.530
And it's expanding faster and faster.

578
42:18.530 --> 42:22.458
Maybe somewhere out there, UFOs

579
42:22.458 --> 42:24.050
could actually exist.

580
42:24.765 --> 42:26.958
Oh, wow, I see...

581
42:26.958 --> 42:31.738
We can't rule out the possibility of alien life.

582
42:31.738 --> 42:34.067
- They could even be watching us right now! - Wow...

583
42:34.067 --> 42:36.710
Doesn't that amaze you, Mi Young?

584
42:38.794 --> 42:41.502
Isn't the very idea of "normal"

585
42:41.502 --> 42:45.150
a little too Earth-centric?

586
42:45.150 --> 42:47.078
I mean, from an alien's perspective,

587
42:47.078 --> 42:51.290
what would humans on Earth look like?

588
42:51.290 --> 42:53.074
So, Mi Young,

589
42:53.074 --> 42:56.010
- shall we go stargazing today? - Stars?

590
42:56.010 --> 42:59.162
My aunt, who was ready to find love again,

591
42:59.162 --> 43:02.470
decided to put that search on hold.

592
43:02.470 --> 43:04.914
You poor, unlucky woman...

593
43:09.774 --> 43:12.780
At last, I had the ordinary relationship I'd always wanted,

594
43:12.780 --> 43:15.591
free from anyone else's interference.

595
43:16.338 --> 43:18.749
Yeon Su! I'm here.

596
43:18.749 --> 43:20.571
You're back?

597
43:21.650 --> 43:23.466
You're almost done, huh?

598
43:23.466 --> 43:26.914
Done? No way. I'm just getting started.

599
43:26.914 --> 43:30.370
Good grief. When am I going to unpack all this?

600
43:30.370 --> 43:31.370
Aren't you hungry?

601
43:31.370 --> 43:34.494
- I am. Since we moved, so jjajangmyeon... - I'll make you aglio e olio.

602
43:34.494 --> 43:36.698
No, jjajangmyeon.

603
43:36.698 --> 43:38.346
Wait.

604
43:38.346 --> 43:42.378
No, please, jjajangmyeon! Let's eat jjajangmyeon.

605
43:42.378 --> 43:43.679
You don't like jjajangmyeon?

606
43:43.679 --> 43:46.080
No, sorry.

607
43:49.730 --> 43:52.994
Oh, this is lubricant, and as you can see here...

608
43:52.994 --> 43:55.422
Here, if you look at it like this...

609
43:55.422 --> 43:57.674
Yes. Hello!

610
43:57.674 --> 44:01.410
Is this your first time in a store like this? Oh, I see. In that case...

611
44:01.410 --> 44:06.142
- Yes, go ahead and touch it. - We have a separate gift bag for it.

612
44:08.974 --> 44:10.290
Take a break if you're tired.

613
44:10.290 --> 44:12.130
No way. We're busy.

614
44:12.130 --> 44:14.498
- Let's get something good to eat after work. - Like what?

615
44:14.498 --> 44:16.470
Beef!

616
44:16.470 --> 44:19.498
Hey, why are you tagging along on their date?

617
44:19.498 --> 44:22.582
Since the boss won't go on blind dates, I'm not getting enough meat.

618
44:22.582 --> 44:24.362
Let's all eat together later.

619
44:24.362 --> 44:26.150
No!

620
44:26.894 --> 44:28.546
The three of you can eat.

621
44:28.546 --> 44:30.234
Okay, thank you.

622
44:30.234 --> 44:32.186
Thank you.

623
44:32.186 --> 44:35.388
Let's go! You got the card.

624
44:43.478 --> 44:47.866
Is this your first time using a product like this?

625
44:50.022 --> 44:51.690
Yes.

626
44:51.690 --> 44:55.590
For beginners, these two are the easiest to use.

627
44:55.590 --> 44:59.502
This one uses air pulses for gentler stimulation.

628
44:59.502 --> 45:01.662
And this one has more precise settings.

629
45:01.662 --> 45:07.038
Oh, then which one would you recommend?

630
45:07.038 --> 45:10.164
Have you... tried them yourself?

631
45:10.910 --> 45:13.142
And then, I realized.

632
45:13.142 --> 45:16.021
What exactly does sex mean to you, Ms. Gong Yeon Su?

633
45:16.021 --> 45:18.806
Why is your perspective on sex so narrow-minded?

634
45:18.806 --> 45:22.230
The question I'd been searching for

635
45:22.230 --> 45:24.322
had no fixed answer to begin with.

636
45:24.322 --> 45:27.002
Then I'll take this one!

637
45:27.002 --> 45:29.658
Sure. I'll bag it for you.

638
45:29.658 --> 45:31.686
Thank you.

639
45:40.226 --> 45:43.710
The answer keeps changing depending on the experiences

640
45:43.710 --> 45:46.784
I fill my life with.

641
45:50.429 --> 45:53.694
It's been ages since I've been here.

642
45:53.694 --> 45:56.354
You said back then that you never know

643
45:56.354 --> 45:59.218
how things between people will turn out.

644
45:59.218 --> 46:01.842
And look at us now.

645
46:01.842 --> 46:04.234
Looks like you won, Ms. Gong Yeon Su.

646
46:04.234 --> 46:05.902
What?

647
46:05.902 --> 46:10.010
That day, when I first looked into your eyes...

648
46:12.310 --> 46:14.520
Now you're looking me in the eye.

649
46:15.230 --> 46:19.442
I think my feelings had already begun back then.

650
46:22.614 --> 46:26.073
Then shall we call it even?

651
46:27.622 --> 46:31.642
For me, it started that day.

652
46:31.642 --> 46:34.707
The day we first kissed.

653
46:47.018 --> 46:48.946
So, speaking of which,

654
46:48.946 --> 46:52.975
there's something I've never once considered doing in my life

655
46:53.738 --> 46:55.561
that I want to try.

656
46:56.586 --> 46:58.394
What?

657
47:04.646 --> 47:06.966
- Ms. Gong Yeon Su. - Wait, wait!

658
47:06.966 --> 47:08.970
W-Why are you doing this?

659
47:08.970 --> 47:10.834
W-Wait, hold on a second!

660
47:10.834 --> 47:12.720
Wait! Hold on...

661
47:16.750 --> 47:22.938
You know I still don't want to get married.

662
47:22.938 --> 47:28.090
I'm so, so happy with what we have right now.

663
47:28.090 --> 47:34.201
I don't want to lose this moment because of the institution of marriage.

664
47:34.201 --> 47:37.103
You understand... right?

665
47:40.398 --> 47:42.817
It's just a couple ring.

666
47:43.914 --> 47:46.284
I was just trying to do something I'd never considered before:

667
47:46.284 --> 47:48.214
get couple rings.

668
47:48.214 --> 47:51.075
I'd love that! Couple rings.

669
47:53.574 --> 47:55.513
Let me put yours on.

670
47:58.810 --> 48:01.419
How is it? Does it fit?

671
48:09.522 --> 48:11.334
Wait!

672
48:20.254 --> 48:21.956
It's pretty.

673
48:23.062 --> 48:24.766
It looks lovely.

674
48:31.114 --> 48:33.460
Let's get one too!

675
48:33.460 --> 48:34.798
This is my first time.

676
48:34.798 --> 48:36.595
Really?

677
48:37.258 --> 48:39.006
Over here!

678
48:41.066 --> 48:43.410
- This one. - This one? Sounds good!

679
48:43.410 --> 48:45.234
Okay! Taking a picture!

680
48:45.234 --> 48:47.566
- Like this! - No, like this! Like this!

681
48:47.566 --> 48:49.717
You have to do it like this!

682
48:53.974 --> 48:55.130
Three!

683
48:55.130 --> 48:58.778
Wait, what's that?

684
48:58.778 --> 49:03.330
You read my mind, didn't you? You did, didn't you?

685
49:23.986 --> 49:25.638
Hey, Yeon Su!

686
49:25.638 --> 49:29.498
You look like you could pull off a triple axel. Didn't expect this!

687
49:29.498 --> 49:31.698
No, the ice here is just terrible.

688
49:31.698 --> 49:34.637
Let's go sledding next time instead.

689
49:35.506 --> 49:37.515
I'm heading out first.

690
49:42.486 --> 49:44.194
Oh, I'm sorry. Are you okay?

691
49:44.194 --> 49:45.854
Oh, yes. I'm fine.

692
49:45.854 --> 49:49.314
- I didn't see you. I'm sorry. - It's fine.

693
49:50.566 --> 49:51.662
- Honey! - Huh?

694
49:51.662 --> 49:53.656
Are you okay?

695
49:57.898 --> 49:59.581
Are you okay?

696
50:00.302 --> 50:02.666
I'm fine! Shall we skate together?

697
50:02.666 --> 50:04.018
- Aren't you hungry? - Not at all.

698
50:04.018 --> 50:06.418
I'm having so much fun!

699
50:11.154 --> 50:12.609
Oh! Hold on tight!

700
50:12.609 --> 50:13.652
Hold on, hold on.

701
50:13.652 --> 50:14.984
I think I'm getting the hang of it now.

702
50:28.994 --> 50:30.525
Here.

703
50:32.003 --> 50:33.213
Thank you.

704
50:33.213 --> 50:35.162
Can I have a bite of this too?

705
50:35.162 --> 50:37.508
Yeah, of course.

706
50:44.266 --> 50:45.542
I should've ordered this.

707
50:45.542 --> 50:46.866
- Want to switch? - No, no.

708
50:46.866 --> 50:48.678
I'm good.

709
50:51.762 --> 50:53.841
Yeon Su, wait...

710
51:19.946 --> 51:21.298
There were days when I thought

711
51:21.298 --> 51:24.574
- marriage was the finish line of love. - Don't we look alike?

712
51:24.574 --> 51:28.560
- An uncertain future scared me back then. - You're right.

713
51:28.560 --> 51:30.344
Wait.

714
51:32.298 --> 51:33.962
You're putting on quite a lot, huh?

715
51:33.962 --> 51:36.300
Of course! So soft.

716
51:37.638 --> 51:41.326
But now, I know.

717
51:41.326 --> 51:46.810
That today's butterflies make me a little stronger tomorrow.

718
51:48.346 --> 51:51.766
Just as our bodies knew we'd fall in love

719
51:51.766 --> 51:53.886
when we first kissed,

720
51:53.886 --> 51:58.739
when the time comes to get married, we'll know then too.

721
52:00.238 --> 52:02.322
Until then, we can keep building

722
52:02.322 --> 52:05.496
our present as we wait for the future.

723
52:17.470 --> 52:19.234
Shall I turn off the light?

724
52:31.250 --> 52:33.961
To make me tingle.
